

1.  Makefile
-----------------------------------
all	- produces hello binary
clean	- removes .o and binary files
hello	- produces hello binary

- use clang: CC=clang
- use flags: CFLAGS= -Wall -Wextra -Werror -pedantic



2. Source Files
-----------------------------------

hello.c:
- write "Hello World!" to stdout when invoked
- PROHIBITED:
	fwrite(), fread()
	put (fptuc, putc, putc unlocked,
		putchar, putchar unlocked, and putw)
	get (fgetc, getc,getc unlocked, getchar,
		getchar unlocked, and getw)
	functions like system(3), that allow you to
		execute external programs.

attestation.txt:
- "I successfully created and am using an Ubuntu 24.04 virtual machine."

None of: BINARY, OBJECT (.o)



3. Clang-Format
-------------------------------------
all .c and .h files are formatted by .clang-format file

Run the following command:
clang-format -i -style=file <filename>
clang-format -i <filename>
